<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4259" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">āthlētĭcus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀθλητικός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to the
			athlete</i>, <i>athletic</i> (not in Cic.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">victus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 4,
					6 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ars,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 15, 16, 2</span></i>
			; also without ars: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">āthlētĭca</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>the athletic
			art</i>, <i>athletics</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 56,
				57, § 205</span></i>.—<i>Adv.</i>:
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">āthlētĭcē</span></b> , <i>athletically</i>, only in Plaut.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pancratice atque athletice (valuit),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Bacch. 2, 3, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Valet pugilice atque athletice,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Ep. 1, 1, 18</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
